course: dictionary
lesson: 989
title: Informal words: bod
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bod is a casual, friendly word, mostly used in Britain. You will meet it in stories and in speech, but not in school writing. «He's a bit of an odd bod, isn't he?» The words around bod tell you what it means.
explain: When bod means a person, the sentence is usually about what someone is like. An odd bod is a strange person, and a nice bod is a pleasant one. Check with a swap: «He's a bit of an odd person» still makes sense, so bod means person here.
explain: Bod is also slang for body, especially a fit or good-looking body. «He's got a fit bod from all that swimming» is about his body, not his character. Always ask what the sentence is describing, then try your meaning in it.
explain: «Dog's body» comes from dogsbody, a person who does the dull jobs nobody else wants. Bod can sound cheeky, so use it when you speak, but choose a clearer word when you write.
fact: A bod is an informal word, mostly used in the UK.
fact: «Bod» means a person when it is used in phrases like «an odd bod».
fact: «Bod» is slang for body, especially a fit or good-looking body.
fact: «Dog's body» means a person who does dull jobs, from «dogsbody».
fact: Informal words sound friendly or a bit cheeky, so keep them out of school writing.
exercise: Grandma says, «Who is that odd bod in the corner?» What is an odd bod? | *A strange person | A small dog | A bowl of soup | A noisy car
exercise: Mum says, «Ellie does all the dull jobs; she's the dog's body.» What does dog's body mean? | A dog's bed | A tired pet | *A person who does dull jobs | A very loud dog
exercise: «He's got a fit bod from all that swimming.» What does bod mean here? | A book | A bird | A bottle | *A body, especially a fit one
test: «The new boy is a nice bod, always helping others.» What does bod mean here? | A bottle | A bookshop | *A person | A body of water
test: Why should you not write bod in a school essay? | *It is informal slang, so it is not used in school writing | It means something rude in every case | Only teachers are allowed to use it | It is too long
exam: In «He's a bit of an odd bod», which word can replace bod and keep the same meaning? | Sandwich | Holiday | *Person | Window
